WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
Speaker 1: There are some reports getting&nbsp;
significant traction that the Department of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:11.680
Justice is deliberately waiting until after&nbsp;
the midterm election to indict Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:18.720
in order to not be seen as making this&nbsp;
political in order to affect the midterms. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:25.040
a lot of common sense applied to the circumstances&nbsp;
suggests that it's not likely Trump would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:31.120
indicted before the midterms anyway. And I'll&nbsp;
tell you why in a moment. A couple of different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:38.240
reports here. DOJ likely to wait past the&nbsp;
midterms to reveal any Trump charges. That's from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:44.560
Bloomberg's Chris Strohm. Federal prosecutors are&nbsp;
likely to wait until after the November election&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:51.440
to announce any charges against Trump if they&nbsp;
determine that he broke laws. Business Insider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.760
Reporting. If prosecutors decide to indict Trump,&nbsp;
they'll wait until after the November midterms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.800
based on a report. The move would be&nbsp;
in accordance with longstanding policy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:09.360
that bars prosecutors from taking overt steps that&nbsp;
could affect the outcome of an election. Attorney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.840
General Merrick Garland also recently introduced&nbsp;
new restrictions to, quote, maintain public&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:20.000
trust in the DOJ. So there's a couple of different&nbsp;
things that I think are important to mention here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:28.720
First of all, Donald Trump isn't on any ballot,&nbsp;
so it's a particular layer removed to if what is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.120
happening here is the DOJ is saying we're going to&nbsp;
bring charges, but not until after the election.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:39.920
Trump is not actually on any ballot, so it would&nbsp;
be better to just do the job that you're trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:46.640
to do. Stop going so out of your way. Not to&nbsp;
be political, because at the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.120
when you're investigating current or former&nbsp;
elected officials, you're not going to avoid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:56.240
allegations that it is political in some sense.&nbsp;
Now, if Donald Trump were on the ballot, if Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:01.600
Trump were running for something in November&nbsp;
and two weeks before he is charged with a crime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:08.320
although it still could be completely correct and&nbsp;
apolitical. We've gotten all the evidence. We've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:14.480
gotten all the as Sean HANNITY calls it, the I's&nbsp;
crossed and the T's dotted, and we're ready to go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:20.080
if that's the timing, to deliberately wait&nbsp;
until after the election. That actually seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.480
more politically motivated than just charging&nbsp;
when you're ready to charge. But that's not the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.640
case here because Trump's not even on the ballot.&nbsp;
So if this were the calculation that were being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:34.800
made by the DOJ, it is a very indirect thing where&nbsp;
it's well, even though Trump's not on the ballot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:40.160
there are members of his party on the ballot&nbsp;
and people that he has endorsed on the ballot.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.400
So let's wait. I would be completely&nbsp;
against that. But I actually think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:52.080
this entire narrative may not be accurate. And the&nbsp;
reason I say that is. It does take a while to put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:59.520
together charges and according to people familiar&nbsp;
with what's going on. Eight and a half weeks for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:06.080
charges. They just got a huge chunk of documents.&nbsp;
It's now September, in August, weeks ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:15.440
It is often the case that it takes months after&nbsp;
search warrants are served to finalize. What are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:22.160
all the charges. Now, without a doubt, when the&nbsp;
FBI decides we're going into the home of a former&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:27.520
president, which they don't often decide, arguably&nbsp;
this is the first time it's happened, you'd better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:34.400
damn well be sure that they already know likely&nbsp;
charges that are on the other end of this and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:39.760
know exactly what they're looking for and what&nbsp;
they believe took place. But at the same time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.960
you've got to go through every document. You have&nbsp;
to see the legal implications of every document&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:50.000
that's there. Later, I'm going to tell you about&nbsp;
multiple Trump associates who believe there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:55.200
more documents or there are copies of documents&nbsp;
that Donald Trump still has stashed elsewhere. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:01.680
so it's not particularly realistic to think that&nbsp;
within ten weeks of getting the documents to begin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:07.200
with, you're already going to be charging Donald&nbsp;
Trump. So while I completely disagree with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.080
idea of deliberately waiting to file charges until&nbsp;
after the election because Trump's not even on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:17.520
ballot, I totally disagree with that. If that is&nbsp;
what is going on, it seems more likely to me that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:23.200
the timeline is going to extend beyond the first&nbsp;
week of November anyway. And I do believe we will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:27.920
see an indictment, but I think it's going to come&nbsp;
later. Now, when we see the indictment, it will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:32.080
very interesting to see how Trump's lawyers react.&nbsp;
And we have a little bit of a preview of that.

